- Support for MHD at the CXL topology level, Redfish modeling is pretty much done - some missing links.
- Support for SSL (https://...)
- DCD: map MCTP Event Notifications to the sending EID instead of draining every DCD; Task support for add/release
- Support GFD
- Support BG commands/context
- Users of cxl-fmd (authentication)
- State for mock topologies.
- Testing, testing, testing.
- OpenBMC integration: bmcweb is the only Redfish service on an OpenBMC
  BMC, so a second service root on another port is not reachable from
  it. Export the topology and DCD state as D-Bus objects (interfaces
  proposed to phosphor-dbus-interfaces, Add/Release Capacity as methods,
  PropertiesChanged on extent updates) and add bmcweb handlers that
  render them. Until then cxl-fmd stays self-contained; bmcweb Redfish
  aggregation (one satellite, prefixed IDs) is the interim option:
  https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/master/docs/AGGREGATION.md
